From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: files dropped or pasted into Linux apps arrive as
 their paths

Files dragged or copied from Files (or Chrome) into a window of a NickelOS
Linux app arrived as nothing. Those apps are clients of Chrome's default
Wayland server, whose security delegate (ChromeSecurityDelegate) knows no
VM for them, and ShareAndTranslateHostToVM ignored clients without a VM:
on ChromeOS only VMs (through their own delegates) and ARC receive files.
On NickelOS the default server's clients are Linux apps running on the
device itself, as the session user, on the same files: they get the
file's own path as a file: URL, nothing to share or translate.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc
index ff2020575c8d2..729f3c4dc68ff 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc
@@ -217,8 +217,12 @@ void ShareAndTranslateHostToVM(
         continue;
       }
     } else {
-      // Ignore unknown VMs
-      continue;
+      // NickelOS: no VM. Only the default Wayland server's clients get here
+      // (ChromeSecurityDelegate knows no VM for them), and on NickelOS those
+      // are Linux apps running on the device itself, as the session user,
+      // on the same files: they get the file's own path. (ChromeOS ignored
+      // these: only VMs and ARC received files.)
+      file_url = ui::FilePathToFileURL(info.path);
     }
     file_urls.push_back(std::move(file_url));
     if (share_required && !share_path->IsPathShared(vm_name, info.path)) {
